# SEO on every page change

Public routes need unique title, description, and a **per-page** canonical. Never set a homepage canonical on the root layout.

- Helpers live in `src/lib/seo.ts` (`getSiteUrl`, `noIndexRobots`, `spotPageTitle`, JSON-LD builders).
- Index: `/` and `/spots/[id]`. Noindex: `/login`, `/spots/new`, `/spots/mine`, `/spots/[id]/edit`, `/auth/*`, `/api/*`.
- New public URLs go in `sitemap.ts` (via `listSpots()`, not `/api/spots`) and must not be `disallow`ed in `robots.ts`.
- Map lists that are virtualized in the client still need server-rendered links (`HomeSpotIndex`).
- Spot pages keep an `h1` and `spotJsonLd`. JSON-LD only through `JsonLd`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — inherited by every route
export const metadata = { alternates: { canonical: "https://after-the-sun.vercel.app" } };

// ✅ GOOD — homepage only
export const metadata = { alternates: { canonical: "/" } };
```
